sre-oncall: Alert — sudden rise in 429s from eu-west-1 GPU fleet starting ~14:02 UTC. SDK telemetry shows retry amplification on many clients.
alert-bot: INCIDENT: queue depth > 75% on rgpu-pool-3 (eu-west-1). Autoscaler suppressed due to noisy multi-tenant jobs.
maria: seeing a bunch of responses with `X-RI-Queue-Length` and `X-RI-Approx-Wait` headers. Example: `X-RI-Queue-Length: 120`, `X-RI-Approx-Wait: 420` (ms). Clients currently ignore them.
kevin: infra change rolled out: admission controller will emit `X-RI-Suggested-Retry` (seconds) and `X-RI-Admission-Token` (short lease id) behind a feature flag. Can SDK consume these?
jonathan: yes — suggestion: SDK should honor `X-RI-Suggested-Retry` and reduce client retries when Approx-Wait > 200ms. Default policy: max_retries=2, exponential backoff with full jitter, and respect `Retry-After` if present.
sdk-dev: I'll open a PR to add a "backpressure-aware" retry policy and a telemetry opt-in flag `backpressure_enabled`. Plan: parse headers `X-RI-Queue-Length`, `X-RI-Approx-Wait`, `X-RI-Suggested-Retry`, `X-RI-Admission-Token` and surface as metrics.
maria: also propose per-region token-bucket limiter in the SDK to prevent retries from amplifying regional hot spots. Start with a conservative default (50 rps) and expose env var override.
kevin: infra will add `X-RI-Capacity-Id` header so clients can correlate which capacity pool returned the response. Also emit `X-RI-Pool-Saturation` (percentage).
jonathan: emphasize: do NOT increase retries by default. We've seen retries multiply load during past incidents. For immediate mitigation set env `RW_SDK_RETRY_MAX=1` for critical customers.
sre-oncall: rolling a soft stop on non-essential training jobs in eu-west-1 to free GPUs. Will post update in ~5m.
alert-bot: INFO: node rgpu-7 removed from pool for thermal; estimated recovery 18m. Autoscaler queued 2 replacement nodes (pending quota).
sdk-dev: example parsing + usage (pseudo):
```
// on response
let qlen = parseInt(res.headers['x-ri-queue-length'] || '0');
let waitMs = parseInt(res.headers['x-ri-approx-wait'] || '0');
let suggested = parseFloat(res.headers['x-ri-suggested-retry'] || '0');
if (waitMs > 200 || qlen > 50) {
  // reduce retries, emit telemetry, back off before retrying
  retryPolicy.maxRetries = Math.min(retryPolicy.maxRetries, 2);
  await sleep(withFullJitter(Math.max(suggested, 100)));
}
// emit telemetry tags: backpressure=true, backpressure.wait_ms=waitMs, backpressure.queue_len=qlen
```
maria: add telemetry fields `backpressure.reason` (e.g., pool_saturation, node_failure), and `backpressure.estimated_wait_ms`. That will help correlate to infra events.
kevin: cost note — if we throttle too aggressively client-side some customers will hit app timeouts and open support tickets. We should coordinate defaults with account management for enterprise tiers.
jonathan: action items: 1) sdk-dev open PR for backpressure-aware retry + token-bucket limiter; 2) infra enable `X-RI-*` headers behind FF and emit `X-RI-Capacity-Id` + `X-RI-Pool-Saturation`; 3) oncall continue node remediation and monitor queue depth; 4) product/ops to review customer-facing defaults.
sre-oncall: +1. I'll keep this thread updated. Please avoid flipping retry defaults in prod until we have telemetry and a rollback plan. :thumbsup:
